The attached image (Figure 5B from Lu et al., Journal of Controlled Release 204 (2015)) is a flow cytometry histogram illustrating the enhanced uptake of FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when adsorbed to Nano-11 nanoparticles. After a 2-hour incubation, BMDCs exposed to soluble OVA alone show a modest increase in OVA fluorescence. In contrast, cells incubated with OVA adsorbed to Nano-11 (Nano-11+OVA) exhibit a significantly pronounced shift to higher fluorescence intensity, indicating a substantial increase in intracellular OVA. This demonstrates Nano-11's effectiveness as a vaccine delivery vehicle, considerably improving antigen internalization by dendritic cells compared to soluble antigen.